        "A. $ -45° $",
        "B. $ 135° $",
        "C. $ 225° $",
        "D. $ 315° $"
      ],
      "correctIndex": 1,
      "hints": [
        "Positive angles rotate counterclockwise.",
        "Quadrant II is between 90° and 180°."
      ],
      "feedbackIfWrong": "Counterclockwise rotation to Quadrant II gives an angle between 90° and 180°. So $ 135° $ is correct."
    },
    {
      "id": "quiz-q2",
      "type": "short-answer",
      "prompt": "If an angle has a measure of $ -200° $, in which quadrant does its terminal side lie? (Answer with a Roman numeral: I, II, III, or IV)",
      "answer": "II",
      "hints": [
